    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch11-03: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.79";
    dc:description "The claim supplies a quantitative relation between measurable ratios and spiral angle. Existing accretionary hard parts retain growth histories, allowing standard geometric tests across representative shells and horns.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Estimate local longitudinal and transverse accretion rates from successive growth increments and test whether their ratio is constant and predicts a constant-angle logarithmic centerline. Variable ratios should predict systematic departures from logarithmic form.";
